    "body": "Adds `gh-pr-pdf`, a command that turns the pull requests of a GitHub repository (and optionally its Discussions) into searchable org files and one paginated PDF, so a codebase's history can be studied as plain text.\n\n```\ngh-pr-pdf siainbuletin/dotfiles\n```\n\n## Changes\n- New Stow package `gh-pr-pdf/`: the script at `gh-pr-pdf/.local/bin/gh-pr-pdf` (links to `~/.local/bin/gh-pr-pdf`) and `gh-pr-pdf/README.org` (usage, needs, safety, \"Not run\"; Stow's default ignore list skips the README).\n- The script wraps `github-backup` for the raw JSON (description, conversation, reviews, inline review comments, commits), writes `org/pr-NNNNN.org` per pull request in number order plus `org/all.org`, then `pandoc -t typst` and `typst compile` make the PDF.\n  - Each org file has a property drawer (`:PR_NUMBER:`, `:STATE:`, `:AUTHOR:`, `:URL:`) for org-ql, and every commit is a link to `github.com/OWNER/REPO/commit/<sha>`.\n  - Options: `--discussions`, `--skip-fetch`, `--no-pdf`, `--per-pdf N`, `--reverse`, `--private`, `-o DIR`.\n  - Pull request text comes from strangers, so raw HTML is dropped, `pandoc` runs with `--sandbox`, and lines starting with an org directive (`#+INCLUDE:` and so on) become literal text. Checked with an injected `#+INCLUDE: \"/etc/passwd\"`.\n- `stow-migration/packages.tsv`: one row (`gh-pr-pdf\tall\t.local/bin/gh-pr-pdf`) so the package is in the list `migrate.sh` derives for each machine. It matches no file in `$HOME`, so it should not change what the migration moves.\n\n## Not run\nWritten in a container without Typst or network access to GitHub's API. Run on made-up JSON: the org and Typst-source output, including headings inside bodies, empty bodies, numeric ordering, `--per-pdf` and the Discussions renderer. Not run:\n- `typst compile`: the PDF itself has not been seen. Try `gh-pr-pdf siainbuletin/dotfiles` and open the PDF; without `typst` it stops after writing the `.typ` file and says so.\n- `github-backup` on a real repository. The JSON key names the script reads (`comment_regular_data`, `comment_data`, `review_data`, `commit_data`) are from memory. If a pull request reports commits but no commit list is found, the script warns and prints the keys it saw; the fix is the key names in `render_pr`.\n- The Discussions fetch (`gh api graphql`), which reads up to 100 comments and 50 replies per discussion and warns on more.\n- `stow gh-pr-pdf` (no Stow in the container): expect `~/.local/bin/gh-pr-pdf` as a symlink into `~/dotfiles/gh-pr-pdf/.local/bin/`.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edit, per the nightly-tidy rule.\n\n---\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi91AWH6eASFA8xAktp)_",
